From cda5f6e33511799ad184cb409d260d50b3d54f42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:32:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FFNY rollback: skip stale sound-stream notes (audio thread
 crash at 0x801E7FC8 / 0x801E7F6C)

Robert's friend session of 29 October: the client's audio thread crashed at 0x801E7FC8 in fight 10, right after a
Blazin' activation. Reproduced in the lab (scripted 10-fight menus-mode sessions with loopback rollbacks: fight 4,
frame 21410, same crash with the old and the new music cue rule; never without rollback). The music module resets
the music stream (0x801E8BAC, cue 0x0002 at a Blazin' activation): its chunks go to the free list and one empty chunk
waits for the disc. Mixer notes for the old buffer (queue 0x803EC9C0 / 0x803EC9C4, run by 0x801E72E0) - queued before
the reset or still arriving for a few mixer passes after it, since the generation byte does not change - then act on
the new buffer: "bytes played" walks into chunk NULL (0x801E7FC8), "buffer done" reads a reused buffer header
(0x801E7F6C).

Now every note is checked where 0x801E72E0 calls its handler (0x801E7344 / 0x801E735C): "bytes played" only if the
stream holds that many bytes, "buffer done" only if the buffer's header still leads back to the same stream, and notes
queued before a reset of their stream are dropped (0x801E8BCC / 0x801E7370). Backstop: 0x801E7F90 drops a "bytes
played" note bigger than the buffered data. Chat reports for the first 3 cases per session; count in the fight-over
lines. Audio-thread state only. FFNY_RB_NOSTREAMGUARD=1 = off. Lab: 2 x 10 fights with the guard, no crash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BJerRaaLvLkg48YnrownjE
